@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Why
+
+The app should show how old a task is and what changed recently. The list does not record when a task was created or last changed, so the app has nothing to show.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- On `add` the two are equal.
+- Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging a task sets its `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- The clock is supplied from outside the domain (the domain may not read the wall clock). `createTodoList` accepts an optional clock for tests and defaults to the system clock.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-timestamps`: creation and last-change times on every task.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts` (Task shape and task operations), `src/domain/list.ts` (clock injection), `src/index.ts` (default clock), `test/list.test.ts`, README.
+- No new dependencies. The public `Task` type gains two fields.
